<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Antemoro</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Antaimoro</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Antemoro (Antaimoro) are a Malagasy people of south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madagascar">Madagascar</a>, around the Matitana river and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vohipeno">Vohipeno</a>. Their ruling clans, who claim descent from Muslim immigrants, established a kingdom around 1500, and their scribes preserved the sorabe, Malagasy texts written in Arabic script. Antemoro diviners were sought after at other Malagasy courts, and the people are known today for Antemoro paper.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/antemoro.jpg" alt="Antemoro" width="320" height="248" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Heinonlein · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Antaimoro-papier,_Ambalavao_05_(cropped).JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
